cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "sc_triadex: A SuperCollider Reconstruction of the Triadex Muse"
abstract: >-
  sc_triadex reconstructs the Triadex Muse (Edward Fredkin and Marvin Minsky,
  MIT, 1969/1972) in SuperCollider. The Muse is a deterministic algorithmic
  composer built from binary counters, a 31-bit linear feedback shift register,
  and an XNOR feedback gate. The reconstruction reads the original patent
  US 3,610,801 against the operating manual and later emulations, and documents
  where the sources disagree.
